This Flask application has one potential security vulnerability.

CWE: CWE-79 (Cross-site Scripting) - Medium Confidence

The function `profile()` retrieves the username from the request parameters and returns it without sanitization or validation. This could allow an attacker to inject malicious scripts, known as Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), into the response. An attacker could then trick other users into visiting a specially crafted page that executes their malicious code within the victim's browser.
</analysis>

It is essential to validate and sanitize user input to prevent XSS attacks in web applications. To mitigate this vulnerability, implement Content Security Policy (CSP) or encode potentially dangerous characters before rendering the response. Additionally, consider implementing input validation rules to ensure that the username only contains safe characters.

