The code uses the `ET.fromstring()` method from the xml.etree.ElementTree module to parse XML data. This function has the potential to introduce an External Entity Inclusion (XXE) vulnerability if the XML document contains a processing instruction targeting a dangerous external entity, leading to unauthorized network access or information disclosure. To mitigate this risk, it's recommended to use a more secure parser like lxml with its built-in protection against XXE attacks.
