   The `getRecord()` function uses `parse(data)` to split the input data, but it does not validate whether the result is valid. If an attacker submits a malicious string that causes the parser to produce unexpected results (e.g., multiple values), the function may return incorrect or misleading information.

3. CWE-269: Improper Handling of Exceptional Conditions:
   Although there are no explicit try/except blocks in this code, if an error occurs during the execution of `parse(data)` or any other operation that could raise an exception (e.g., invalid input type), it may not be properly handled. This can lead to a denial-of-service (DoS) condition if an attacker can manipulate the system into raising frequent exceptions.

