   CWE-22 (Path Traversal) - Medium Confidence: The function uses the `os.path.exists()` method to check if the file exists, which may lead to path traversal attacks if not properly sanitized. An attacker could use directory traversal characters (`..`, `/`) in the file name to access parent directories or other files on the system.

   CWE-97 (Improper Handling of Path Separators) - Low Confidence: Although the function uses `os.path.exists()` method, it does not check for path separators like `/` or `\`. An attacker could use a directory separator in the filename to manipulate the file path and access unauthorized areas of the filesystem.

